 Conejos River and\nthe Rio Grande, including Del Norte and Mogote.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood http://cotrip.org","ends":"2026-11-02T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c43837866a64e434d490f547f232ecfdd4c91f85.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c43837866a64e434d490f547f232ecfdd4c91f85.001.1"},{"event":"Winter Storm Watch","headline":"Winter Storm Watch issued October 31 at 4:17AM MDT until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Heavy snow possible. Total snow accumulations between 8 and\n14 inches possible. Winds could gust as high as 55 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Feet.\n\n* WHEN...From Sunday afternoon through Monday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult, especially Sunday night\nand Monday morning. Strong winds could produce areas of blowing and\ndrifting snow.","ends":"2026-11-02T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.de2a76b3205083779bf3095183d6bd237c3d91ba.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.de2a76b3205083779bf3095183d6bd237c3d91ba.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 30 at 3:02PM MDT until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and southeast\nUtah, including the following areas, Canyonlands/Natural Bridges,\nLa Sal and Abajo Mountains and Southeast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...From late Saturday night through Monday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recently burned areas, and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- 1 to 3 inches of rain is expected across portions of southeast\nUtah and southwest Colorado from Sunday morning through Monday\nmorning over soils that are still saturated from recent rainfall\nand flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-02T11:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d9e2fd526e1e61f9532cd34833bc42a40d097b54.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d9e2fd526e1e61f9532cd34833bc42a40d097b54.001.1"},{"event":"Winter Storm Watch","headline":"Winter Storm Watch issued October 30 at 12:22PM MDT until November 2 at 12:00PM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Heavy snow possible above 10,000 feet. Total snow\naccumulations between 10 to 15 inches with locally higher amounts\npossible. Winds could gust as high as 40 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Northwest San Juan Mountains and Southwest San Juan\nMountains.\n\n* WHEN...From Sunday morning through noon Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult.","ends":"2026-11-02T13:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e28a7beacf0d23c29b492575ceef0ca347b3ac8f.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e28a7beacf0d23c29b492575ceef0ca347b3ac8f.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-31T11:37:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 311137 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 537 AM MDT Sat Oct 31 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Showers continue through Friday night. Lower